mats-qemu: QEMU for the Mats virtual target

The archives this repository publishes hold qemu-system-arm and the shared
libraries it loads, built from upstream source releases with the patches
in patches/ (one, to GLib's configure on macOS), which ship in the sources
bundle too. Each component keeps its own licence:

  QEMU           GPL-2.0-only (some files under compatible licences; see
                 its LICENSE)
  dtc (libfdt)   GPL-2.0-or-later OR BSD-2-Clause, linked into QEMU
  GLib           LGPL-2.1-or-later
  PCRE2          BSD-3-Clause WITH PCRE2-exception
  libffi         MIT
  zlib           Zlib
  proxy-libintl  LGPL-2.0-or-later (the macOS and Windows archives only)

Each licence's text is in the archive's licenses/<component>/ folder.

Source: every release qemu-<version>-<n> of
https://github.com/haoliu0419/mats-qemu carries
mats-qemu-<version>-<n>-sources.tar.xz, which holds each component's
upstream tarball exactly as built, every patch, and the scripts and
workflow that built that release's archives. It stays published for as
long as the release does. The repository's own scripts are under the
GPL-2.0 (LICENSE).

GLib, PCRE2, libffi, zlib and proxy-libintl are linked dynamically: each is
a separate file in the archive that can be replaced by a build of the same
library from its source.
